& [SJS]
  + Situation: exact and relation proposals are indexed and proof-carrying while legacy lexical recall rescans every unit using substring containment and an additive score
  + Justification: Cantor needs fast term association without importing substring false positives scalar score laundering or a second authority store
  + Solution: derive a separately rooted lexical posting sidecar from admitted text then use typed token evidence and exact coverage arithmetic only as a lower-tier proposal channel

& [CompletedWorkSupportReview]
  + Slice2 provides exact address label meaning-reference package source and fabric-root identity
  + Slice3 provides candidate accumulation exact gates PriorityLattice budgets pagination and whole-result replay
  + Slice4A provides typed contribution accounts result association grouping and a pattern for channel-specific evidence forms
  + direct query proves the minimum legacy lexical surface is preferred expression aliases and meaning text
  + direct query substring matching additive scores Instant elapsed checks and full-unit scan are rollback observations not reusable authority
  + Slice4A lacks its full completion proof so this review cannot issue implementation authority

& [PrimaryArchitectureDecision]
  + recommend a DerivedLexicalAssociationIndex sidecar keyed by exact catalogue_root fabric_root tokenizer profile compiler identity and index_root
  + do not add postings to SemanticAnchorCatalogue or change its source-of-truth status
  + do not force exact-only callers to construct use or trust a lexical index
  + exact scanner bytes and behavior remain a callable rollback path
  + a lexical-enabled entry point must explicitly receive and validate the sidecar

& [ConceptualModel]
  + LexicalSurfaceKind is PreferredExpression Alias or Meaning
  + LexicalPosting binds normalized token exact SemanticAddress surface kind surface digest evidence identities and occurrence account
  + DerivedLexicalAssociationIndex binds sorted token-to-posting sets to exact catalogue and fabric roots
  + LexicalTermAccount binds original term normalized tokens and whether an earlier exact channel resolved it
  + LexicalMatchAccount binds candidate query tokens matched tokens postings surfaces coverage calculation and index root
  + AssociationContribution carries a lexical match account only when channel is Lexical and no relationship path

& [RecommendedTokenizerProfile]
  + [profile] cantor-lexical-tokenizer/0.1
  + trim the complete surface then apply Unicode lowercase and split at characters the compiled standard library classifies as non-alphanumeric
  + discard empty runs deduplicate tokens in sorted order and retain original text plus exact surface digest separately
  + perform no stop-word deletion stemming lemmatization synonym expansion edit distance n-gram generation Unicode normalization or confusable folding
  + bind tokenizer profile compiler identity and fixture digest because Unicode classification and lowercase tables are toolchain behavior
  + include ASCII punctuation mixed-case combining-mark composed-decomposed non-Latin numeric one-character and empty-token adversarial fixtures before activation

& [IndexDerivation]
  + exact-rebuild the Slice2 catalogue against the same admitted SemanticFabric before indexing
  + index preferred_expression and aliases from each IdentityAnchorEntry
  + exact-resolve meaning text from the corresponding admitted SemanticUnit and verify the already-derived meaning_ref correspondence
  + derive a domain-separated surface digest before tokenization
  + emit one canonical posting per token unit surface kind and surface digest while counting repeated occurrence separately without rank inflation
  + sort tokens postings identities surfaces and evidence then compute index_root and whole-artifact proof digest
  + mutation or absence of profile compiler roots address surface text meaning reference token posting order or digest refuses

& [QueryEligibility]
  + form the lexical-eligible term set only from query terms not resolved by an enabled ExactIdentity or ExactLabel stage
  + tokenize each eligible original term and retain a per-term account even when it yields no token
  + free-form subject purpose use case boundary and criteria fields do not become lexical input
  + look up the union of postings for unique eligible query tokens
  + exact-resolve every posting target against the same catalogue and fabric then apply the unchanged Slice3 lifecycle authority purpose use-case and boundary gate
  + a lexical proposal never bypasses a gate or seeds declared applicability or typed relation traversal in Slice4B

& [CoverageArithmetic]
  + candidate matched tokens are the set intersection between all unique lexical-eligible query tokens and tokens evidenced by that candidate postings
  + relevance_basis_points is floor of matched_token_count times ten-thousand divided by eligible_query_token_count
  + matched count must be positive total count must be positive and checked integer arithmetic must not overflow
  + duplicate terms tokens occurrences aliases or surfaces never increase matched unique-token count
  + surface kind occurrence count token order meaning length field prestige and exact-channel evidence add no numeric weight
  + same coverage remains a tie and the existing winning-tier ambiguity rule applies
  + higher exact applicability and relation tiers remain lexicographically prior regardless of lexical coverage

& [BudgetAndCompleteness]
  + recommend AnchorBudget maximum_lexical_postings as a new channel-specific bound
  + determine the complete posting union cardinality before candidate mutation
  + if it exceeds the bound return BudgetTooSmall or LexicalBudgetExceeded without partial candidates because the existing cursor cannot resume incomplete discovery
  + after complete bounded aggregation sort lexical candidates by coverage descending then stable exact address
  + contribute to already-present higher-tier candidates without consuming a new candidate slot
  + add only the strongest remaining new lexical candidates that fit the complete page-continuation candidate capacity and mark lower-tier candidate clipping explicitly
  + wall-clock time remains unobserved in the deterministic operator

& [RootAndProfileBoundary]
  + a lexical result must commit the lexical index root as machine data rather than only prose
  + recommend a lexical-enabled scanner profile and cursor profile distinct from cantor-exact-anchor-scan/0.1
  + recommend a new public lexical entry point sharing pure internal gates and assembly while leaving scan_exact_semantic_anchors callable and byte-stable
  + activation must choose a versioned result-root carrier or wrapper that does not silently reinterpret old exact result bytes
  + embedding and learned artifacts may later use a generalized proposal-artifact-root map but Slice4B must not pre-authorize them

& [LegacyCorrespondence]
  + preferred expression alias and meaning surfaces correspond to legacy scope
  + exact identity and exact label overlap must remain equal under Slice3 and later Slice4C fixtures
  + lexical score equality with legacy additive substring behavior is neither expected nor desirable
  + explicit regression fixtures should show substring-only cases such as short token inside an unrelated longer token no longer propose

& [FaultModel]
  + LexicalIndexRootMismatch for stale catalogue fabric tokenizer compiler or index identity
  + LexicalPostingMismatch for token surface address evidence occurrence or order disagreement
  + LexicalProfileUnsupported for unknown tokenizer or lexical scanner profile
  + LexicalBudgetExceeded before partial discovery
  + LexicalMatchMismatch for term token posting coverage or candidate disagreement
  + LexicalScoreLaundering for value outside exact coverage formula or any cross-channel conversion
  + LexicalResultMismatch for absent extra or mutated index-root commitment under canonical replay

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + fold_1 preserves user purpose canonical Slice4 claim Slice4A state and legacy implementation evidence
  + fold_2 separates authoritative records exact catalogue lexical sidecar proposal evidence gates and ranking
  + fold_3 models tokenizer surfaces postings index root term accounts match accounts budget and faults
  + fold_4 traces every token through surface digest address package meaning reference and admitted fabric root
  + fold_5 prunes substring fuzzy stop-word synonym embedding learning subject inference wall-clock and authority arithmetic
  + fold_6 forms rebuild mutation duplicate Unicode budget gate tie ordering and rollback fixtures
  + fold_7 converges on a sidecar compiler typed evidence lower-tier query stage and separate profile without code activation
  + [gain_delta] query work becomes posting lookup over a compiled semantic surface while every association still resolves to exact source-bearing identity

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty keeps token coverage labeled as lexical relevance and preserves originals ties absence and false-positive regression
  + Security binds sidecar roots compiler profile budgets exact gates and distinct entry-point authority
  + Weaver composes query token to posting to candidate associations but receives no selection or admission authority
  + Planner orders exact resolution gates complete posting accounting rank and pagination without partial discovery
  + Refiner uses one minimal surface family and unique-token formula without fuzzy features
  + Scribe records each surface digest token posting term match score equation omission and root
  + Observer compares fresh sidecar rebuild canonical query replay legacy exact overlap and measured corpus behavior

& [ActivationPrerequisites]
  + Slice4A reserved completion proof and signature exist
  + tokenizer Unicode and compiler-version policy is explicitly accepted in preserved activation source
  + lexical sidecar versus embedded-index decision is retained as sidecar
  + exact-only byte compatibility and lexical result-root carrier are specified
  + maximum_lexical_postings bounds and failure semantics are added to closed query forms
  + adversarial fixture matrix is phase-locked before code

